course: dictionary
lesson: 5128
title: Invert: turning things round
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To invert something is to turn it upside down, or to swap it round so it goes the opposite way. Think of a pancake flipped over in the pan. «The photo was inverted, so the trees pointed at the ground.» The trees pointing at the ground tells you the picture was turned upside down.
explain: Invert can also mean a change of order, back to front or in reverse. Read the words around it: if something has been flipped, the sentence will show it was the other way round from normal. When you meet invert, ask: what has been turned round? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Invert appears in many subjects. In maths, to invert a fraction is to turn it upside down. In science, a lens can invert an image. In English, a question inverts the subject and verb, as in «Is he coming?» Each time, the direction or order has been flipped.
explain: Inverted commas are a different use of the word. They are quotation marks that hug someone's exact words, like «Hello,» said Sam. They are also called speech marks. Single ('...') and double ("...") inverted commas are both correct, but use one kind consistently.
fact: Invert means to turn something upside down, or to swap it round so it goes the opposite way.
fact: In maths, to invert a fraction means to turn it upside down: 2/3 becomes 3/2.
fact: Inverted commas are quotation marks, also called speech marks, that show a character's exact words.
fact: The punctuation that ends the spoken words goes inside the closing inverted commas.
fact: Both single ('...') and double ("...") inverted commas are correct; many UK books use single and US books use double.
exercise: «The photo was inverted, so the trees pointed at the ground.» What does inverted mean here? | Made much bigger | Taken at night | Blurred and out of focus | *Turned upside down
exercise: In «"Hello," said Sam», what do the inverted commas show? | The words Sam is thinking silently | That the sentence is a question | That Sam is shouting | *The exact words Sam says
exercise: Which sentence has its subject and verb inverted, like a question? | He is coming. | *Is he coming? | Coming he is now. | He will come soon.
test: In «She inverted the list so the oldest name came first», what does inverted mean? | *Swapped round so the order is reversed | Written in pencil | Read out loud | Lost on the way to the office
test: Which of these is another name for inverted commas? | *Speech marks | Full stops | Hyphens | Brackets
exam: A lens can invert an image; what does this mean? | It makes the picture brighter | It removes the colour from the picture | *It turns the picture upside down or back to front | It cuts the picture into two halves
